/T (The size of the UnitedStates Supreme Court is not fixed by the Constitution, it is set by ordinary legislation passedbyCongress, and it has changed seven times across American history. Since 1869, the number hasstoodatnine Justices, a norm now over a century and a half old \(Wikipedia contributors\). Thisissueasks a deceptively simple question with enormous consequences: should Congress amend theJudiciary Act of 1869 to change that number, and if so, under what conditions is doing so a legitimateactofgovernance rather than a partisan power grab? )
