/Title (The Chair presides as Vice President of the Senate and votesonly to break a tie, the Co-Chair presides as President pro tempore only when the Chair is absent, otherwise voting as a regular delegate. Resolutions pass on a floor vote alone, with a cloture threshold \(currently being finalized\) required to close debate before any final vote is taken. The conference runs across two days and eight working sessions in total.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1110 0 R
/Prev 1228 0 R
/Next 1229 0 R
>>
endobj
1297 0 obj
<<
/Title (The size of the UnitedStates Supreme Court is not fixed by the Constitution, it is set by ordinary legislation passedbyCongress, and it has changed seven times across American history. Since 1869, the number hasstoodatnine Justices, a norm now over a century and a half old \(Wikipedia contributors\). Thisissueasks a deceptively simple question with enormous consequences: should Congress amend theJudiciary Act of 1869 to change that number, and if so, under what conditions is doing so a legitimateactofgovernance rather than a partisan power grab?)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1230 0 R
/Next 1310 0 R
>>
endobj
1298 0 obj
<<
/Title (Unlike many international committees, this is not a question of resolving conflict between nations; it is a question of institutional self-restraint. The Senate holds the legal power to change the Court's size at any time; the entire debate is whether it should.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1230 0 R
/Prev 1310 0 R
>>
