/Title (However, unlike usual legislative controversies, the argument here cannot be only about the making of national policy; it is more important than that, as it raises fundamental questions about democratic representation itself. The Senate has constitutional powers in accordance with Article I, Section 4 to change state laws dealing with congressional elections and the question now is whether the Senate should utilize these powers in order to introduce national standards.)
