/Title (The only serious historical attempt to expandthe Supreme Court remains Roosevelt's 1937 plan. Frustrated that the Court had repeatedly struck down New Deal legislation as unconstitutional, Roosevelt proposed allowing the President to appoint one additional Justice for every sitting Justice over the age of seventy, up to a maximum of six new seats, potentially expanding the Court from nine to fifteen \(Grassley/Senate Judiciary Committee\). He justified this publicly by claiming the Court was overwhelmed with cases, a claim Chief Justice Charles Evan Hughes directly refuted before Congress \(Fox News\).)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1344 0 R
/Next 1365 0 R
>>
